/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f128a886574e5ea88775535ff930828ec5090d4f.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued September 15 at 6:32PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"At 632 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 12\nmiles north of Fruita, or 18 miles northwest of Grand Junction,\nmoving east at 20 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and half inch hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nThis storm will remain over mainly rural areas of northwestern Mesa\nCounty.","ends":"2026-09-15T19:00:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Roan and Tavaputs Plateaus; Grand Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1c30a46c0a4d80ffb4e827140d8823c0af2678a9.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1c30a46c0a4d80ffb4e827140d8823c0af2678a9.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-16T00:17:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 160017 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 617 PM MDT Tue Sep 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - There is a chance for strong to severe storms over the next few days, capable of producing hail, gusty winds, and heavy rainfall. - Moderate to heavy rainfall could lead to localized flash flooding, rockfalls, and mudslides at times this week. - Flood Watc","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-15T19:00:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Critical fire weather conditions will not be met as subtropical moisture continues to feed into the 4 Corners and Central Rockies region this week. Daily and nightly shower and thunderstorm activity can be anticipated with some storms producing gusty outflow winds and containing moderate to heavy rainfall rates. Widespread wetting rainfall appears l